{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Checks a Python command without running it: regenerates its source from the store, then, in a separate Python process (the venv next to data/ if present), compiles it, imports it as the runtime would (missing packages, errors in imports or module-level code), and type-checks it with mypy against the ndata_py/flowlang stubs when mypy is installed in that Python. Returns {status, command, file, interpreter, python, mypy: 'ran'|'not installed', clean, problems: [{tool: 'python'|'import'|'mypy', severity, where, line, message}]} - `where` is the author's own line: 'body line N' or 'imports line N'. clean is false when any problem is an error; status is 'err' only when the check cannot run (not a Python command, no interpreter). Use it after upsert_command / patch_command_body on a Python command.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::buildrust::build;\nuse flowlang::pycmd::check;\nuse std::path::Path;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"tgzgxv1a19e04dfe3g1","readers":[],"time":1793652514996,"username":"system","writers":[]}